# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
#   https://github.com/hoffmangroup/segway/issues/22
# Symptom: BED12 where the last block does not reach chromEnd; the spec
#   requires that chromStart + blockStarts[last] + blockSizes[last] == chromEnd.
#   A mismatch arises when a converter applies thickEnd instead of the last
#   exon end for the final block boundary, or when a soft-clip was applied to
#   the transcript end.  UCSC bigBed converter rejects with "blocks don't
#   reach end of bed element".
# Format: chrom start end name score strand thickStart thickEnd itemRgb blockCount blockSizes blockStarts
chr1	1000	5000	tx1	0	+	1200	4800	0	3	200,300,400	0,1500,3200
chr2	10000	20000	tx2	0	-	10200	19500	0	3	300,500,400	0,4000,8000
